**M00.DecodeHeader:** Independent implementation and production upgrade acceptance; decoding is not admission.

**M00.DecodeTransaction:** No nonce reservation or balance authority from decoded bytes.

**M01.VerifyWork:** Fastest-adversary work cost, public ingress fairness and complete native host remain unqualified.

**M01.VerifyTransactionSignature:** Component signature parity does not establish independent cryptographic acceptance.

**M02.AdmitBlock:** Native consensus actor and hostile public network are not implemented by the reference owner.

**M02.ChooseBranch:** No independent network security or work-hardness acceptance.

**M03.RunWorkAttempt:** Selector uses real mining to construct reorg inputs only; durable miner, stale-job cancellation and publication reconciliation remain unimplemented.

**M03.EnterExternalEffect:** Entry is not actual dispatch, target-side exactly-once, final-use authority or coherent rollback protection.

**M04.ReadFrame:** Exact retained native transport and proof-admission components are not the ordinary peer service; no current registered per-procedure network test.

**M04.PropagateVerifiedBlock:** Historical network/host reports are separate observations; no source-equal byte check makes a new WAN or independent-operator run.

**M05.ValidateTransaction:** Native mempool reservation and ordinary peer event wiring remain separate.

**M05.ReconsiderAfterReorg:** New-generation nonce/funds rechecking must connect to mempool events; existing execution tests do not demonstrate resubmission or physical-effect reconciliation.

**M06.ExecuteCandidate:** Compressed in-memory root updates are not native paged persistence; full maps, 16 MiB bridge bounds and complete native host remain open.

**M06.DeriveBranchDelta:** No separate native branch store is implied by reusable local MVCC persistence.

**M07.OpenNamespace:** Native paged state owner, full descriptor/sidecar fencing and physical power loss remain open.

**M07.StageBranch:** Root rejection and admission/restart tests are not independent disk durability acceptance.

**M08.PlanReorg:** Full fork lists/staging copy remain reference limits; public immutable plan API and bounded native planning are absent.

**M08.RecoverAndPublish:** Physical power loss, native long runs and external-effect compensation remain unaccepted.

**M09.ValidateArtifact:** Not arbitrary large-model loading, model provenance or a public export grant.

**M09.FetchWithoutAuthor:** Current zero-adoption E3 run is not a new author-loss/DA campaign; use historical artifacts for their actual scope. Independent long-term custodians and repair remain open.

**M10.SubmitContribution:** Bounded windows are not public economic Sybil fairness or authentic task provenance.

**M10.PublishEvaluatedRelease:** Synthetic signed release transitions are not three improving public-model generations.

**M11.EvaluateFrozenModel:** Future-window, independent evaluator, provenance and poisoning acceptance remain open.

**M11.AdmitEvaluation:** First-two attestation policy is not objective ML truth, evaluator independence or ledger work.

**M12.ClaimContributionReward:** No monetary-value, fairness or external payout reconciliation claim.

**M12.ConsumeSponsoredQuota:** Real GPU availability, delivery evidence, sponsor self-traffic and sustainable funding remain separate.

**M13.RebuildBranchState:** Checkpoint/spool tests do not demonstrate native paged WAN synchronization or long-term archival economics.

**M13.VerifyIncomingHistory:** Controlled file/stdio delivery with receiver-verified block cursors; not a persistent native WAN node, succinct proof, independently operated network or global-freshness guarantee.

**M14.QueryCurrentState:** Not a succinct light client or proof of latest global tip; public discovery, eclipse defense, ordinary Hepta authority and native node assembly remain unintegrated.

**M14.ConsumePublishedModel:** Not an ordinary Hepta destination, a final-use token or a proof of actual provider delivery.

**M15.StartExecutableSpecPeer:** Native node startup and ordinary product entry are absent; historical loopback/owned-host experiments retain their exact sources.

**M15.StopAndReconcile:** Child cleanup tests do not prove full node shutdown, durable miner stop or physical target reconciliation.

**M16.TrainCompatibleCandidate:** Training executions are retained campaign observations, not a unit-test result or real future user-task generation.

**M16.CompareOrAbstain:** Three no-update attempts do not establish prospective improving generations.

**M17.CheckDetailedContracts:** Current checker-source changes need their own executed PR checks; historic source-contract logs are not proof of this checker revision.

**M17.QualifyExecutedCampaign:** Does not execute old tests again, confer scientific independence or grant deployment authority.

